    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## DVD: video depth in one pass\n\n[DVD](https://github.com/EnVision-Research/DVD) (Deterministic Video Depth, EnVision Research) is Wan 2.1 T2V 1.3B retrained to regress depth: clean video latents in, depth latents out, one forward pass, no sampling, no text encoder. ComfyUI runs Wan 2.1 natively, so the converted weights load with the stock loaders and **DVD Video Depth** runs the pass with DVD's windowing and window alignment.\n\n**Models** (put each in the folder shown)\n\n| File | Folder | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| `dvd_1.1_bf16.safetensors` | `models/diffusion_models` | [nynxz/DVD](https://huggingface.co/nynxz/DVD) |\n| `wan_2.1_vae.safetensors` | `models/vae` | [Comfy-Org/Wan_2.1_ComfyUI_repackaged](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Wan_2.1_ComfyUI_repackaged/tree/main/split_files/vae) |\n\n**Settings**\n\n- `height` x `width` 480 x 640: the frames are scaled to cover this box (aspect kept) and the depth is resized back. This is DVD's reference setting; bigger is slower and off-distribution.\n- `window_size` 81 / `overlap` 21: frames per pass and the frames shared by consecutive windows, where they are aligned (scale + shift) and cross-faded. DVD's demo settings. Lower the window for less VRAM.\n- `normalize` video: one min/max for the whole clip, so the scale stays consistent across frames. `turbo` colours it. Near is bright; `invert` flips that.\n- About 7 GB of VRAM and 6 s per 81-frame window at 480 x 880 on an RTX 5090 (fp16).\n"
   ],
   "title": "DVD Video Depth"
  }
